/* ---- VEX only, long mode: AVX, AVX2, FMA, F16C, BMI1, BMI2 (docs/MMU4K.md, section 4.1). Like the VEX rows
 * above, they leave out a vector register in VEX.vvvv; By is a general register there. VSIB (gathers),
 * VMASKMOV/VPMASKMOV, EVEX and XOP have no rows: no form, so nothing runs them but the CPU itself. */
/* VMOVSS/VMOVSD: from or to memory they leave vvvv unused, between registers they merge from it. */
